#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:172
#, no-wrap
msgid "Alternatives to WINE"
msgstr "WINE 的替代品"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:175
msgid "For FreeBSD users, some alternatives to using WINE are as follows:"
msgstr "对于 FreeBSD 用户，可以使用以下方法代替使用 WINE："

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:177
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Dual-Booting: A straightforward option is to run desired Windows(R) "
"applications natively on that OS. This of course means exiting FreeBSD in "
"order to boot Windows(R), so this method is not feasible if access to "
"programs in both systems is required simultaneously."
msgstr "双启动：一种简单直接的选择是在 Windows(R) 系统上原生运行所需的应用程序。当然，这意味着必须退出 FreeBSD 才能启动 Windows(R)，因此，如果需要同时访问两个系统中的程序，这种方法就不适用了。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:186
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Virtual Machines: Virtual Machines (VMs), as mentioned earlier in this "
"chapter, are software processes that emulate full sets of hardware, on which "
"additional operating systems (including Windows(R)) can be installed and "
"run.  Modern tools make VMs easy to create and manage, but this method comes "
"at a cost. A good portion of the host systems resources must be allocated to "
"each VM, and those resources cannot be reclaimed by the host as long as the "
"VM is running. A few examples of VM managers include the open source "
"solutions qemu, bhyve, and VirtualBox. See the chapter on crossref:"
"virtualization[virtualization,Virtualization] for more detail."
msgstr "虚拟机：如本章前文所述，虚拟机（VM）是模拟完整硬件集的软件进程，可在其上安装并运行其他操作系统（包括 Windows(R)）。现代工具让虚拟机易于创建和管理，但这种方法需要付出代价。主机系统的相当一部分资源必须分配给每台虚拟机，并且只要虚拟机在运行，主机就无法收回这些资源。虚拟机管理器包括开源解决方案 qemu、bhyve 和 VirtualBox。有关详情，请参阅 crossref:virtualization[virtualization,虚拟化]章节。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:187
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Remote Access: Like many other UNIX(R)-like systems, FreeBSD can run a "
"variety of applications enabling users to remotely access Windows(R) "
"computers and use their programs or data. In addition to clients such as "
"xrdp that connect to the standard Windows(R) Remote Desktop Protocol, other "
"open source standards such as vnc can also be used (provided a compatible "
"server is present on the other side)."
msgstr "远程访问：与许多其他类 UNIX(R) 系统一样，FreeBSD 可以运行各种应用程序，让用户远程访问 Windows(R) 计算机并使用其程序或数据。除了连接到标准 Windows(R) 远程桌面协议的 xrdp 等客户端外，也可以使用 vnc 等其他开源标准（前提是另一端运行兼容的服务器）。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:189
#, no-wrap
msgid "Installing WINE on FreeBSD"
msgstr "在 FreeBSD 上安装 WINE"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:192
msgid "WINE can be installed via the pkg tool, or by compiling the port(s)."
msgstr "WINE 可以使用 pkg 或 Ports 安装。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:194
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "WINE Prerequistes"
msgid "WINE Prerequisites"
msgstr "WINE 相关依赖"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:197
msgid ""
"Before installing WINE itself, it is useful to have the following pre-"
"requisites installed."
msgstr "在安装 WINE 之前，需要安装这些东西。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:199
msgid "A GUI"
msgstr "GUI"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:203
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Most Windows(R) programs are expecting to have a graphical user interface "
"available.  If WINE is installed without one present, its dependencies will "
"include the Wayland compositor, and so a GUI will be installed along with "
"WINE.  But it is useful to have the GUI of choice installed, configured, and "
"working correctly before installing WINE."
msgstr "大多数 Windows(R) 程序都需要图形用户界面。如果安装 WINE 时系统中没有图形界面，其依赖项将包括 Wayland 合成器，因此 WINE 安装时也会一并安装图形界面。不过，最好在安装 WINE 之前先安装、配置并确保所选图形界面正常运行。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:205
msgid "wine-gecko"
msgstr "wine-gecko"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:211
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The Windows(R) operating system has for some time had a default web browser "
"pre-installed: Internet Explorer.  As a result, some applications work under "
"the assumption that there will always be something capable of displaying web "
"pages.  In order to provide this functionality, the WINE layer includes a "
"web browser component using the Mozilla project's Gecko engine.  When WINE "
"is first launched it will offer to download and install this, and there are "
"reasons users might want it do so (these will be covered in a later "
"chapter).  But they can also install it prior to installing WINE, or "
"alongside the install of WINE proper."
msgstr ""
"<trademark class=\"registered\">Windows</trademark>操作系统已经预装了浏览器 "
"Internet Explorer。因此，一些应用程序在工作时假设总有一些能够显示网页的东西。"
"为了提供这个功能，WINE层包含了一个使用Mozilla项目的Gecko引擎的网页浏览器组"
"件。当WINE第一次启动时，它将提供下载和安装这个组件，而且用户可能希望它这样做"
"的原因（这些将在后面的章节中介绍）。但是他们也可以在安装WINE之前安装它，或者"
"在安装WINE的同时安装。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:213
msgid "Install this package with the following:"
msgstr "使用以下方法安装包："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:217
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# pkg install wine-gecko\n"
msgstr "# pkg install wine-gecko\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:220
msgid "Alternately, compile the port with the following:"
msgstr "或使用 Port 套件集安装："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:225
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# cd /usr/ports/emulators/wine-gecko\n"
"# make install\n"
msgstr "# cd /usr/ports/emulators/wine-gecko\n# make install\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:228
msgid "wine-mono"
msgstr "wine-mono"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:231
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "This port installs the MONO framework, an open source implementation of "
#| "Microsoft's .NET. Including this with the WINE installation will make it "
#| "that much more likely that any applications written in .NET will install "
#| "and run on the system."
msgid ""
"This port installs the MONO framework, an open source implementation of "
"Microsoft's .NET.  Including this with the WINE installation will make it "
"that much more likely that any applications written in .NET will install and "
"run on the system."
msgstr ""
"这个移植程序会安装MONO框架，这是微软的.NET的一个开源实现。在安装 WINE 的同"
"时， 将它与 WINE 一起安装， 可以使任何用 .NET 编写的应用程序更容易在系统上安"
"装和运行。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:233
msgid "To install the package:"
msgstr "要安装套件可："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:237
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# pkg install wine-mono\n"
msgstr "# pkg install wine-mono\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:240
msgid "To compile from the ports collection:"
msgstr "从Port套件集安装："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:245
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# cd /usr/ports/emulators/wine-mono\n"
"# make install\n"
msgstr "# cd /usr/ports/emulators/wine-mono\n# make install\n"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:248
#, no-wrap
msgid "Installing WINE via FreeBSD Package Repositories"
msgstr "使用 pkg 安装 WINE"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:251
msgid ""
"With the pre-requisites in place, install WINE via package with the "
"following command:"
msgstr "有了先决条件，用下面的命令通过 pkg 安装WINE："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:255
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# pkg install wine\n"
msgstr "# pkg install wine\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:258
msgid "Alternately compile the WINE sub-system from source with the following:"
msgstr "或使用以下方法从源码编译 WINE 子系统："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:263
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"# cd /usr/ports/emulators/wine\n"
"# make install\n"
msgstr "# cd /usr/ports/emulators/wine\n# make install\n"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:266
#, no-wrap
msgid "Concerns of 32- Versus 64-Bit in WINE Installations"
msgstr "32 位和 64 位的区别"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:271
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Like most software, Windows(R) applications made the upgrade from the older "
"32-bit architecture to 64 bits.  And most recent software is written for 64-"
"bit operating systems, although modern OSes can sometimes continue to run "
"older 32-bit programs as well.  FreeBSD is no different, having had support "
"for 64-bit since the 5.x series."
msgstr "与大多数软件一样，Windows(R) 应用程序也从较旧的 32 位架构升级到了 64 位。如今的大多数软件都是为 64 位操作系统编写的，不过现代操作系统有时也能继续运行较旧的 32 位程序。FreeBSD 也不例外，自 5.x 系列起便支持 64 位架构。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:274
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "However, using old software no longer supported by default is a common "
#| "use for emulators, and users commonly turn to WINE to play games and use "
#| "other programs that do not run properly on modern hardware. Fortunately, "
#| "FreeBSD can support all three scenarios:"
msgid ""
"However, using old software no longer supported by default is a common use "
"for emulators, and users commonly turn to WINE to play games and use other "
"programs that do not run properly on modern hardware.  Fortunately, FreeBSD "
"can support all three scenarios:"
msgstr ""
"然而，使用默认情况下不再支持的旧软件是仿真器的常见用途，用户通常会转而使用"
"WINE来玩游戏和使用其他在现代硬件上无法正常运行的程序。幸运的是，FreeBSD可以支"
"持这三种情况："

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:276
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"On modern, 64-bit machine and want to run 64-bit Windows(R) software, simply "
"install the ports mentioned in the above sections. The ports system will "
"automatically install the 64-bit version."
msgstr "如果使用的是现代 64 位计算机，并且想运行 64 位 Windows(R) 软件，只需安装上述章节中提到的 ports。ports 系统会自动安装 64 位版本。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:277
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "Alternately, users might have an older 32-bit machine that they do not "
#| "want to run with its original, now non-supported software. They can "
#| "install the 32-bit (i386) version of FreeBSD, then install the ports in "
#| "the above sections. Again, on a 32-bit machine the ports system will "
#| "install the corresponding 32-bit version of WINE by default."
msgid ""
"Alternately, users might have an older 32-bit machine that they do not want "
"to run with its original, now non-supported software. They can install the "
"32-bit (i386) version of FreeBSD, then install the ports in the above "
"sections."
msgstr ""
"或者， 用户可能有一台较旧的 32 位机器， 但他们不希望用原来的、 现在不支持的软"
"件来运行。他们可以安装32位(i386)版本的FreeBSD， 然后再安装上述章节中的 "
"ports。同样，在32位的机器上， ports系统会默认安装相应的32位版本的WINE。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:279
#, no-wrap
msgid "Running a First WINE Program on FreeBSD"
msgstr "在 FreeBSD 上运行第一个 WINE 程序"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:283
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "Now that WINE is installed, the next step is to try it out by running a "
#| "simple program. An easy way to do this is to download a self-contained "
#| "application, i.e., one can simply unpack and run without any complex "
#| "installation process."
msgid ""
"Now that WINE is installed, the next step is to try it out by running a "
"simple program.  An easy way to do this is to download a self-contained "
"application, i.e., one can simply unpack and run without any complex "
"installation process."
msgstr ""
"现在WINE已经安装好了，下一步就是通过运行一个简单的程序来试用它。一个简单的方"
"法是下载一个自带的应用程序，即可以简单地解压并运行，而不需要任何复杂的安装过"
"程。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:285
msgid ""
"So-called \"portable\" versions of applications are good choices for this "
"test, as are programs that run with only a single executable file."
msgstr ""
"所谓的 \"可移植 \"版本的应用程序（中文里也有成为绿色软件）是这个测试的好选"
"择，只有一个可执行文件运行的程序也是如此。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:287
#, no-wrap
msgid "Running a Program from the Command Line"
msgstr "从命令行运行程序"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:291
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"There are two different methods to launch a Windows program from the "
"terminal.  The first, and most straightforward is to navigate to the "
"directory containing the program's executable ([.filename]#.EXE#) and issue "
"the following:"
msgstr ""
"有两种不同的方法可以从终端启动一个Windows程序。第一种，也是最直接的方法是导航"
"到包含程序可执行文件（<filename>.EXE</filename>）的目录，然后执行以下命令："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:295
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "% wine program.exe\n"
msgstr "% wine program.exe\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:298
msgid ""
"For applications that take command-line arguments, add them after the "
"executable as usual:"
msgstr "对于接受命令行参数的应用程序，像往常一样在可执行文件后添加参数："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:302
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "% wine program2.exe -file file.txt\n"
msgstr "% wine program2.exe -file file.txt\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:305
msgid ""
"Alternately, supply the full path to the executable to use it in a script, "
"for example:"
msgstr "或者提供可执行文件的完整路径来在脚本中使用它，例如："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:309
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "% wine /home/user/bin/program.exe\n"
msgstr "% wine /home/user/bin/program.exe\n"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:312
#, no-wrap
msgid "Running a Program from a GUI"
msgstr "使用 GUI 运行程序"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:316
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"After installation graphical shells should be updated with new associations "
"for Windows executable ([.filename]#.EXE#) files.  It will now be possible "
"to browse the system using a file manager, and launch the Windows "
"application in the same way as other files and programs (either a single- or "
"double-click, depending on the desktop's settings)."
msgstr ""
"安装后，图形 shell 应更新为Windows可执行文件（<filename>.EXE</filename>）的新"
"关联。现在可以使用文件管理器浏览系统，并以与其他文件和程序相同的方式启动"
"Windows应用程序（单击或双击，取决于桌面的设置）。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:319
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"On most desktops, check to make sure this association is correct by right-"
"clicking on the file, and looking for an entry in the context menu to open "
"the file.  One of the options (hopefully the default one) will be with the "
"*Wine Windows Program Loader*, as shown in the below screenshot:"
msgstr "在大多数桌面环境中，可以右键单击该文件并查看上下文菜单中的打开选项，以确认文件关联是否正确。其中一个选项（希望是默认选项）应为 *Wine Windows Program Loader*，如下方截图所示："

#. type: Target for macro image
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:320
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "wine-run-np++-1.png"
msgstr "wine-run-np++-1.png"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:323
msgid ""
"In the event the program does not run as expected, try launching it from the "
"command line and review any messages displayed in the terminal to "
"troubleshoot."
msgstr ""
"如果程序没有按预期运行，请尝试从命令行启动它，并查看终端中的消息以排除故障。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:325
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"In the event WINE is not the default application for [.filename]#.EXE# files "
"after install, check the MIME associate for this extension in the current "
"desktop environment, graphical shell, or file manager."
msgstr ""
"如果WINE在安装后不是<filename>.EXE</filename>文件的默认应用程序，请在当前桌面"
"环境、图形外壳或文件管理器中检查该扩展名的MIME关联。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:327
#, no-wrap
msgid "Configuring WINE Installation"
msgstr "WINE 的安装配置"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:331
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"With an understanding of what WINE is and how it works at a high level, the "
"next step to effectively using it on FreeBSD is becoming familiar with its "
"configuration.  The following sections will describe the key concept of the "
"_WINE prefix_, and illustrate how it is used to control the behavior of "
"applications run through WINE."
msgstr ""
"在对 WINE 是什么以及它的工作原理有了高层次的了解之后，下一步要想在 FreeBSD 上"
"有效地使用它，就要熟悉它的配置。下面的章节将描述<emphasis>WINE前缀</emphasis>"
"概念，并说明如何使用它来控制通过WINE运行的应用程序的行为。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:333
#, no-wrap
msgid "WINE Prefixes"
msgstr "WINE 前缀"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:338
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A WINE _prefix_ is a directory, usually located beneath the default location "
"of [.filename]#$HOME/.wine# though it can be located elsewhere.  The prefix "
"is a set of configurations and support files used by the wine to configure "
"and run the Windows(R) environment a given application needs.  By default, a "
"brand new WINE installation will create the following structure when first "
"launched by a user:"
msgstr "WINE __前缀__是一个目录，通常位于默认位置 [.filename]#$HOME/.wine# 下，但也可以位于其他位置。前缀包含一组配置和支持文件，供 WINE 配置和运行特定应用程序所需的 Windows(R) 环境。默认情况下，用户首次启动全新安装的 WINE 时，会创建以下目录结构："

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:340
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"[.filename]#.update-timestamp#: contains the last modified date of [."
"filename]#file /usr/share/wine/wine.inf#. It is used by WINE to determine if "
"a prefix is out of date, and automatically update it if needed."
msgstr ""
"<filename>.update-timestamp</filename>: 包含<filename>/usr/share/wine/wine."
"inf</filename>的最后修改日期。它被WINE用来判断一个前缀是否过时，并在需要时自"
"动更新它。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:341
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"[.filename]#dosdevices/#: contains information on mappings of Windows(R) "
"resources to resources on the host FreeBSD system. For example, after a new "
"WINE installation, this should contain at least two entries which enable "
"access to the FreeBSD filesystem using Windows(R)-style drive letters:"
msgstr "[.filename]#dosdevices/#：包含 Windows(R) 资源到 FreeBSD 主机系统资源的映射信息。例如，全新安装 WINE 后，该目录至少应包含以下两个条目，以便通过 Windows(R) 风格的驱动器盘符访问 FreeBSD 文件系统："

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:343
#, fuzzy
msgid "[.filename]#c:@#: A link to [.filename]#drive_c# described below."
msgstr "[.filename]#c:@#：指向下文所述的 [.filename]#drive_c# 的链接。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:344
#, fuzzy
msgid "[.filename]#z:@#: A link to the root directory of the system."
msgstr "[.filename]#z:@#：指向系统根目录的链接。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:346
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"[.filename]#drive_c/#: emulates the main (i.e., [.filename]#C:#) drive of a "
"Windows(R) system. It contains a directory structure and associated files "
"mirroring that of standard Windows(R) systems. A fresh WINE prefix will "
"contain Windows(R) 10 directories such as _Users_ and _Windows_ that holds "
"the OS itself. Furthermore, applications installed within a prefix will be "
"located in either _Program Files_ or _Program Files (x86)_, depending on "
"their architecture."
msgstr "[.filename]#drive_c/#：模拟 Windows(R) 系统的主驱动器（即 [.filename]#C:#）。其中包含目录结构和相关文件，与标准 Windows(R) 系统相对应。全新的 WINE 前缀会包含 Windows(R) 10 的目录，例如 _Users_ 和 _Windows_，后者存放操作系统本身。此外，在前缀中安装的应用程序将位于 _Program Files_ 或 _Program Files (x86)_ 中，具体取决于其架构。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/wine/_index.adoc:347
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"[.filename]#system.reg#: This Registry file contains information on the "
"Windows(R) installation, which in the case of WINE is the environment in [."
"filename]#drive_c#."
msgstr "[.filename]#system.reg#：此注册表文件包含有关 Windows(R) 安装的信息；在 WINE 中，它指的是 [.filename]#drive_c# 内的环境。"

#. type: Plain text
